            <div xml:id="d877">

                <pb facs="0932" n="920" sameAs="frus:frus1941v01/pg920"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">611.61/27b: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Ambassador in the Soviet Union</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Steinhardt</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1941-05-23T15:00:00-04:00">May 23, 1941—3
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>722. In thousands of dollars for March, 1941, exports of United States
                    merchandise to the Soviet Union, 3,590; re-exports, 647; imports of merchandise
                    from the Soviet Union for consumption in the United States, 4,264. Three months
                    total for these classifications, 15,423; 978; and 6,889 respectively. All
                    figures are preliminary.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
